      "linked_preview_mission": "py-01",
      "numbered_prompts": [
        {
          "cell": 1,
          "original": "1. Create a variable ```var1``` which contains the value 5"
        },
        {
          "cell": 2,
          "original": "2. Create a variable ```var2``` which contains the value 9.5"
        },
        {
          "cell": 3,
          "original": "3. Create a new variable ```var3``` by multiplying those two variables"
        },
        {
          "cell": 4,
          "original": "4. Use the built-in function ```type(a)``` that returns the type of variable that ```a``` is on ```var1```, ```var2``` and ```var3```. Does it all make sense?"
        },
        {
          "cell": 5,
          "original": "5. Create a variable ```var4``` that contains text with multiple words"
        },
        {
          "cell": 6,
          "original": "6. Use the method ```upper``` attached to ```var4``` that capitalizes all characters"
        },
        {
          "cell": 7,
          "original": "7. Import the ```scikit-image.io``` module"
        },
        {
          "cell": 8,
          "original": "8. Read the image at this address and store the result in a variable: https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Elephant_Diversity.jpg/1920px-Elephant_Diversity.jpg"
        },
        {
          "cell": 9,
          "original": "9. Import the ```import matplotlib.pyplot as plt``` and display the image you just imported"
        }
      ],
      "code_examples": []
    },
    {
      "id": "e02",
      "path": "e02-Numpy_basics.ipynb",
      "url": "https://github.com/guiwitz/PyImageCourse_beginner/blob/master/e02-Numpy_basics.ipynb",
      "linked_preview_mission": "im-01",
      "numbered_prompts": [
        {
          "cell": 1,
          "original": "1. Import Numpy"
        },
        {
          "cell": 2,
          "original": "2. Create a 6 rows, 4 columns array of 1s called ```my_array```. Using the ```shape``` parameter make sure the size is correct."
        },
        {
          "cell": 3,
          "original": "3. Modify the element at row = 3, column = 1 to be 50"
        },
        {
          "cell": 4,
          "original": "4. Modify the array by multiplying all its values by 3"
        },
        {
          "cell": 5,
          "original": "5. Using Google, find the Numpy function to take the square root and create a new array called ```my_array_root``` by applying it to your current ```my_array```."
        },
        {
          "cell": 6,
          "original": "6. Create a new array called ```my_array_sum``` by multiplying ```my_array``` and ```my_array_root```"
        },
        {
          "cell": 7,
          "original": "7. Find the maximum value of your array by using either a methods or a function"
        },
        {
          "cell": 8,
          "original": "8. Create a boolean array where only places in ```my_array_sum``` which are larger than 100 are ```True```."
        },
        {
          "cell": 9,
          "original": "9. Recover all the values in ```my_array_sum``` which are true in the boolean array using logical indexing. What is the shape of the array containing these values?"
        }
      ],
      "code_examples": []
    },
    {
      "id": "e03",
      "path": "e03-More_on_Images.ipynb",
      "url": "https://github.com/guiwitz/PyImageCourse_beginner/blob/master/e03-More_on_Images.ipynb",
      "linked_preview_mission": "im-02",
      "numbered_prompts": [
        {
          "cell": 1,
          "original": "1. Import the numpy and skimage packages"
        },
        {
          "cell": 2,
          "original": "2. Using the skimage import function, load the image visible at this link: http://wiki.cmci.info/sampleimages/cells_Actin.tif\nand put it in a variable called image"
        },
        {
          "cell": 3,
          "original": "3. Check what are the dimensions of the image"
        },
        {
          "cell": 4,
          "original": "4. Check what is the image type. Is it an 8 or 16 bit image ?"
        },
        {
          "cell": 5,
          "original": "5. Plot the image using Matplotlib (that you have to import). Change the color map to 'gray' and make the image larger"
        },
        {
          "cell": 6,
          "original": "6. Plot a histogram of the pixel values. Change the bin size to better see the distribution"
        },
        {
          "cell": 8,
          "original": "1. Make a cropped version of the image by selecting 100 rows for which you want all columns and plot it."
        },
        {
          "cell": 9,
          "original": "2. Select a region in the image of 100x100 pixesl and create a cropped image. Plot it."
        },
        {
          "cell": 10,
          "original": "3. Using this second cropped image, create a boolean mask by finding all pixels above some reasonable threshold (use the histogram above to find a value)"
        },
        {
          "cell": 11,
          "original": "4. Plot your mask"
        },
        {
          "cell": 12,
          "original": "5. Get all the values of all the pixels which are selected in the mask and store in a variable"
        },
        {
          "cell": 13,
          "original": "6. Plot a histogram of all the values"
        }
      ],
      "code_examples": []
    },
