      "path": "e04-Thresholding.ipynb",
      "url": "https://github.com/guiwitz/PyImageCourse_beginner/blob/master/e04-Thresholding.ipynb",
      "linked_preview_mission": "im-04",
      "numbered_prompts": [
        {
          "cell": 1,
          "original": "1. Import the relevant packages: numpy, matplotlib and skimage"
        },
        {
          "cell": 2,
          "original": "2. Import the same image from this url address: https://cildata.crbs.ucsd.edu/media/images/13585/13585.tif"
        },
        {
          "cell": 3,
          "original": "3. Create a new variable called ```image_green``` that contains only the green channel by slicing the array"
        },
        {
          "cell": 4,
          "original": "4. Plot this image"
        },
        {
          "cell": 5,
          "original": "5. Plot a histogram of the image"
        },
        {
          "cell": 6,
          "original": "6. Try to determine an appropriate threshold to recover the large structures in the image, create the corresponding mask and plot it"
        },
        {
          "cell": 7,
          "original": "7. There are other algorithms for thresholding than the one of Otsu. Try to find one in the [Scikit-image documentation](http://scikit-image.org/docs/dev/api/skimage.filters.html) and to use it"
        }
      ],
      "code_examples": []
    },
    {
      "id": "e05",
      "path": "e05-Filtering.ipynb",
      "url": "https://github.com/guiwitz/PyImageCourse_beginner/blob/master/e05-Filtering.ipynb",
      "linked_preview_mission": "im-05",
      "numbered_prompts": [
        {
          "cell": 2,
          "original": "1. Using the skimage documentation (Google it), try to find the Sobel filter. Try it out on ```image_nuclei``` and by plotting it, try to understand what it does"
        },
        {
          "cell": 3,
          "original": "2. Using the Otsu method, make a mask of the filtered image and plot it"
        },
        {
          "cell": 4,
          "original": "3. Threy to erode the image. Use influence regions of different sizes and observe the effect:"
        },
        {
          "cell": 5,
          "original": "4. Choose an erosion level that leaves at least one of the circles complete. Use the skeletonize filter on your resulting eroded mask"
        }
      ],
      "code_examples": [
